N:zeroshot
D:Operate the-open-engine/zeroshot as a safety-first execution control plane for persistent multi-agent software workflows. Route to the established Node product or standalone Rust and Python lane; validate setup graph provider isolation credentials delivery and evidence without paid calls; freeze acceptance and cost; start or resume only after exact approval; monitor durable state; and verify trace or semantic JSONL without exposing content.
G:zeroshot the-open-engine multi-agent coding-agents conductor worktree docker provider-routing pr-delivery auto-merge rust-cli python-sdk trace-jsonl semantic-jsonl

U[8]:
  Assess fit and choose Node zeroshot versus standalone zeroshot-rust or the Python SDK
  Install or update one pinned product after checking host release registry CI and lifecycle scripts
  Validate setup workflow runtime provider isolation credential and delivery plans without a paid run
  Start a bounded software-change workflow only after exact task cost and side-effect approval
  Observe diagnose stop resume or recover a durable run from status ledger worktree and log evidence
  Open a review PR or ship only under separate delivery and merge approvals
  Export and structurally verify trace or semantic JSONL without revealing prompts or raw output
  Extend the owning Node Rust protocol target or Python subsystem with focused verification

S[10]{n,step,details}:
  1,Choose one mode,fit | install | plan | execute | observe | recover | evidence | target | extend; do not turn a read or plan request into mutation
  2,Choose one product,Node owns established setup provider worktree Docker resume export and PR UX; Rust owns typed graphs targets JSON and NDJSON plus Windows; Python is a typed Rust projection and was not on PyPI at audit
  3,Freeze the contract,Record exact version repo base bounded end state acceptance non-goals provider model topology retry limit isolation credential names delivery cost ceiling and approval
  4,Inspect safely,Run scripts/zeroshot.sh doctor; print credential names or SET and MISSING only; setup-plan is read-only and applying settings is separate
  5,Validate and isolate,Run upstream strict config validation or native validate-only; default Node coding to explicit worktree; inspect Docker mounts env Gateway tools web search and target auth
  6,Preflight and approve,Use scripts/zeroshot.sh preflight to print one shell-quoted proposal; it blocks current checkout ship missing Docker provider and forge prerequisites; then wait for explicit approval
  7,Execute exactly,Run only the approved command; any change to task provider model topology retry credentials network isolation delivery or cost requires reapproval
  8,Observe and recover,Read JSON status and bounded logs first; stop before kill; resume means another paid turn; finish means PR plus merge; preserve ledgers and worktrees until resolved
  9,Verify and deliver,Reproduce acceptance from direct files behavior tests and forge state; report whether a distinct validator ran; agent completion and Git state are not proof
  10,Export or extend,Create a new sensitive trace or semantic export and run trace_summary.py; for source changes edit the owning subsystem and run focused Node Rust protocol or Python gates without live paid tests

R[14]:
  Audit pin is 362453b743ca1ef79d4fff3525f9db3cffdbf2ad on 2026-08-27; prefer successful Node v6.45.0 commit f015ffd66465b50613421717c323d14cef23df27 over that failing main push CI
  Native zeroshot-rust-v0.4.0 is independently released; do not mix commands ids state versions or support claims with Node
  Python source advertises pip install zeroshot-rust but PyPI returned 404 and publishing failed at audit; recheck before recommending
  Never start resume finish schedule or another provider turn without explicit provider cost and consequence approval
  No-flag Node resolution can mutate the current checkout; guided setup recommending worktree does not prove the setting was applied
  Ship implies PR and merge behavior; PR implies worktree unless Docker; Docker wins; no-isolation conflicts with PR ship Docker and worktree
  PR approval is not merge approval; finish is a ship operation; read back branch PR merge and issue state from the forge
  Trivial local runs can use one worker with no independent validator; report actual verifier separation rather than a template promise
  CLI providers own authentication; bundled Gateway settings can store an API key and must have narrow file and command tools
  Docker defaults can mount gh git and ssh credentials; worktrees separate files but are not a credential process or network sandbox
  Native runtime JSON lists environment variable names only; named targets can receive GH_TOKEN; direct targets are unauthenticated
  target serve without bootstrap-key-file is unauthenticated; bind local experiments to loopback and require a security plan before exposure
  Logs traces and semantic exports can contain prompts source tool data and provider output; never paste or upload them casually
  Clean purge kill-all force-stop uninstall update schedules provider-live tests and publication each need the matching approval

E[9]{type,command}:
  Install skill,npx skills add https://github.com/akillness/jeo-skills --skill zeroshot
  Read-only doctor,bash .agent-skills/zeroshot/scripts/zeroshot.sh doctor /path/to/repo
  Read-only setup plan,bash .agent-skills/zeroshot/scripts/zeroshot.sh setup-plan /path/to/repo
  Safe run preflight,bash .agent-skills/zeroshot/scripts/zeroshot.sh preflight --repo /path/to/repo --input 'Add JSON output with tests' --isolation worktree --delivery none --provider codex
  Strict config validation,bash .agent-skills/zeroshot/scripts/zeroshot.sh validate-config workflow.json --strict
  Read-only run status,bash .agent-skills/zeroshot/scripts/zeroshot.sh status RUN_ID
  Content-free trace audit,python3 .agent-skills/zeroshot/scripts/trace_summary.py run.trace.jsonl --strict
  Native no-submit validation,zeroshot-rust run --title 'Validate graph' --input input.json --template software-change --uniform-runtime-config runtime.json --validate-only
  Validate skill,bash .agent-skills/skill-standardization/scripts/validate_skill.sh .agent-skills/zeroshot
